WEBVTT

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:12.460
الحمد لله والصلاة والسلام على رسول الله

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:14.100
وعلى آله وصحبه أجمعين

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:17.160
In this session, inshaaAllah, I will explain to you the relationship

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:20.930
between the last ten aayaat of--

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:22.850
last 10 surahs of the Quran.

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:26.940
Just the order of the last 10 surahs of the Quran. We'll go through it quickly.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:31.260
Just so you appreciate-- just that conclusion to that discussion

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:34.110
that the surahs of the Quran are in remarkable order.

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:34.560
Okay.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:38.210
So I'll begin with a Surah al-Fil. Anybody know the beginning of Surah al-Fil?

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:39.682
بِسۡمِ ٱللَّهِ ٱلرَّحۡمَـٰنِ ٱلرَّحِیمِ

00:00:40.546 --> 00:00:42.962
أَلَمۡ تَرَ كَیۡفَ فَعَلَ رَبُّكَ بِأَصۡحَـٰبِ ٱلۡفِیلِ

00:00:42.962 --> 00:00:46.518
What is the surah about? It is about Ka'aba, the Makkah--

00:00:46.542 --> 00:00:51.490
the city of Makkah being attacked by an army of elephants and it being protected.

00:00:51.562 --> 00:00:54.430
Allah (عز وجل) protected that city under any circumstance.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:57.460
Even if it was facing an impossible enemy,

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:00.110
impossible to fight against, an army of elephants, it's--

00:01:00.110 --> 00:01:01.750
Allah still protected that city.

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:04.050
The very next surah is Surah Quraysh.

00:01:04.079 --> 00:01:05.220
How does it begin?

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:07.755
لِإِیلَـٰفِ قُرَیۡشٍ

00:01:07.775 --> 00:01:13.000
Allah (عز وجل) talks about how He took care of the economic prosperity of the city of Makkah.

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:14.840
رِحۡلَةَ ٱلشِّتَاۤءِ وَٱلصَّیۡفِ

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:19.760
They could travel in the winter and in the summer freely. Now

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:23.660
I want to take you back to a du'a. A du'a of Ibrahim (عليه السلام).

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:27.900
Ibrahim (عليه السلام)-- remember he made the du'a, "Make this a peaceful city."

00:01:27.910 --> 00:01:28.660
You remember that?

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:30.520
Okay, I told you

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:35.260
he said, "Make this a peaceful city and provide its children from all kinds of fruit."

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:38.450
And yesterday I told you that the "peaceful city" part

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:42.190
is about its protection and law and order and security.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.760
And then the "fruit" part is about what?

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:48.280
Economic prosperity. Actually, Surah al-Fil and

00:01:48.301 --> 00:01:53.430
Surah Quraysh together are the fulfillment of the du'a of Ibrahim (عليه السلام).

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:58.250
In Surah al-Fil, even if an army of elephants attacks, the city is still safe.

00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:00.370
Allah will protect that city,

00:02:00.395 --> 00:02:04.760
fulfilling the du'a of Ibrahim when he said, "Ya Allah, make the city safe."

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:06.200
Then he said,

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:10.490
"Provide them all kinds of fruit." And Allah says, in the next surah, that the

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:14.930
Quraysh get to go and travel in the summer and in the winter.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:17.860
Now, this is important people because the Quraysh

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:21.150
were the center of Arabian society.

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:26.060
And the Arabs were really, really big on robbing each other to death.

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:29.550
Except they left the Quryash alone.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:32.630
The Quraysh would only-- they could travel whenever they want.

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:35.280
So actually,
what the other people used to do is

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:39.160
they only used to travel during the very difficult hot seasons.

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:44.180
Or very intense cold seasons. They could only travel in those seasons. Why?

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:47.360
Because then they know that the robbers, it's too hard for them to wait

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:50.650
for us in the desert. So we can only travel during the tough times.

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:53.780
So we'll go towards the hot climate in the summer

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:56.060
and we'll go towards the cold climate in the winter.

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:58.920
Even though for convenience, what should you do?

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:01.390
You go towards the cold climate in the summer

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:03.460
and you go towards the hot climate in

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:05.800
the winter. But everybody else couldn't do that.

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:08.410
But the Quraysh could go wherever they want.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:09.550
Free ride.

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:12.350
No problem. Nobody will rob them. Why not?

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:17.050
Because every other tribe used to have idols. And where are the idols stored?

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:18.660
In Makkah.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:21.720
If you mess with them, they'll say, "You took our money.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:24.060
Now, watch what happens when I go back to Makkah."

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:26.390
I'm gonna take that idol of yours and..." [cracking sound]

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:30.590
"You see that giant monkey?

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:33.060
You watch who's tail is missing when you get there?"

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:35.560
You understand?

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:38.310
So they were afraid of messing with

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:40.460
Makkah because the Makkans would then destroy their?

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:42.760
Idols. So they left them alone.

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:49.390
Also, after the entire story of you know, the army of elephants being destroyed.

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:53.390
The Mushrikoon used to believe that the people of Quraysh are untouchable.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:55.020
They are crazy powerful.

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:57.760
You don't mess with them because even elephants can't mess with them.

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:00.740
So we'll leave them alone. So Allah says,

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:02.080
رِحْلَةَ الشِّتَاءِ وَالصَّيْفِ

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:03.430
What's incredible, though, is

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:07.710
Allah says, I made those conveniences for you. You can travel wherever you want,

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:09.770
whenever you want, unlike anybody else.

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:12.450
By the way when they do travel, out of season,

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:15.820
what did they bring back? All kinds of fruits.

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:20.579
They bring back out of season fruits. Nobody else has those fruits. They do.

00:04:20.589 --> 00:04:24.679
What was the du'a Ibrahim? Provide these
people all kinds of fruit.

00:04:24.695 --> 00:04:27.699
وَٱرۡزُقۡ أَهۡلَهُۥ مِنَ ٱلثَّمَرَ ٰ⁠تِ

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:29.260
Provide them all kinds of fruits.

00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:35.260
Then Allah told the Quraysh: I'm providing you everything that Ibrahim asked for.

00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:38.540
You should at least be true to the legacy of your father.

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:43.090
He built that house. Not so you could do shirk. Not so you could worship false gods.

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:45.620
He built that house so you can worship Him.

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:48.340
فَلۡیَعۡبُدُوا۟ رَبَّ هَـٰذَا ٱلۡبَیۡتِ

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:51.790
The reason that house is mentioned - or this house - the Kaaba is mentioned

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:54.560
in that Sura is because the house was built by who?

00:04:55.440 --> 00:05:00.340
Ibrahim. And their prosperity is directly a result of the prayer of Ibrahim.

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:03.050
So everything's actually going back to Ibrahim (عليه السلام).

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:06.560
Do you guys understand the relationship between Surah al-Fil and Surah al-Quraysh?

00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:08.040
One after the other.

00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:11.530
Now that those two surahs have been mentioned together, Allah (عز وجل)

00:05:11.530 --> 00:05:14.010
then mentions in the next Surah, Al-Ma'un:

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:17.650
You people are supposed to fulfill the legacy of Ibrahim.

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:20.760
And instead of fulfilling the legacy of Ibrahim-- by the way

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:22.080
what is the legacy of Ibrahim?

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:23.850
You worship Allah sincerely.

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:26.160
You worship Allah sincerely.

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:27.620
Right?

00:05:27.770 --> 00:05:30.550
And as a result of worshiping Allah sincerely, you serve people.

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:31.960
You do good to people.

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:35.960
Ibrahim (عليه السلام) is very generous. Even when strangers come to his house.

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:36.560
What did he do?

00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:41.150
He takes the best meat that he has. There's a baby cow in the back.

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:42.360
No more.

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:43.930
[cutting sound]

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:47.950
And he gets slaughtered and he feeds them. You know, he's a giving person.

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:50.480
This is generally-- he cares about other people.

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:53.420
Angels come and say, "We're going to destroy the nation of Lut." What does he say?

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:54.550
"Hey, wait, don't do that."

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:56.460
"Take care of those people."

00:05:57.440 --> 00:05:59.680
He's making du'a for humanity he's making du'a

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:05.880
for other people, caring about them. So he's got two
qualities, Ibrahim (عليه السلام). He's really close to Allah.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:08.360
He worships Allah sincerely, and he cares about people.

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:10.550
He really cares about people, right?

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:12.180
The irony is,

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:15.900
you people are supposed to be living up to the legacy of Ibrahim (عليه السلام),

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:17.760
yet, let's see how you measure up.

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:21.490
Let's see what you - meaning the Quraysh - look like. Well,

00:06:21.503 --> 00:06:28.210
أَرَءَیۡتَ ٱلَّذِی یُكَذِّبُ بِٱلدِّینِ. فَذَ ٰ⁠لِكَ ٱلَّذِی یَدُعُّ ٱلۡیَتِیمَ.  وَلَا یَحُضُّ عَلَىٰ طَعَامِ ٱلۡمِسۡكِینِ

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:29.560
Have you seen the one

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:35.150
who lies against the deen altogether? He doesn't encourage the feeding of the poor.

00:06:35.940 --> 00:06:37.950
He pushes the orphan around,

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:39.461
you know?

00:06:39.471 --> 00:06:41.350
فَوَیۡلࣱ لِّلۡمُصَلِّینَ

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:43.520
Then the worst kind of destruction should fall upon

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:46.160
people who pray and pray only to show off.

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:49.860
And when they pray, they're lazy and lackadaisical.

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:52.780
They don't even care what they're praying, how they're praying.

00:06:52.790 --> 00:06:54.760
They're standing in salah, like, you know.

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:57.310
What kind of people are these?

00:06:57.320 --> 00:06:58.380
وَیَمۡنَعُونَ ٱلۡمَاعُونَ

00:06:58.380 --> 00:07:00.880
And they're so cheap. And they're so miserly

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:02.750
they won't even give people [مَاعُون].

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:03.960
Do you know what [مَاعُون] is?

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:06.180
[مَاعُون] is little things.

00:07:06.930 --> 00:07:08.200
Somebody knocks on your door.

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:11.180
You live in an apartment, somebody knocks on your door and says, "Hey,

00:07:11.270 --> 00:07:12.360
do you have salt?"

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:14.760
"We don't know what that is."

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:17.140
[laughs]

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:21.240
It's [مَاعُون], it's not gonna kill you to give them a spoon of salt.

00:07:21.940 --> 00:07:23.800
[scoffs] "Take my salt!"

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:25.840
[laughs]

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:29.050
So Allah is saying, then, in this surah,

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:32.860
the criticism is you people don't pray sincerely and you're so cheap.

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:36.150
Isn't that the exact opposite of what Ibrahim (عليه السلام) represents?

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:40.160
So, first Allah says: I gave you what Ibrahim asked for.

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:43.800
And you're not true to your father's legacy. In Surah al-Ma'un.

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:46.680
Then let's see what happens next.

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:50.560
Well, if you're not true to the
legacy that Ibrahim (عليه السلام)

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:53.290
was supposed to-- well you were supposed to fulfill that legacy.

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:55.060
Maybe there's someone else who does.

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:56.585
The next surah is,

00:07:56.585 --> 00:07:59.430
إِنَّاۤ أَعۡطَیۡنَـٰكَ ٱلۡكَوۡثَرَ

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:00.050
Rasul (صلى الله عليه وسلم).

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:01.610
There--

00:08:01.610 --> 00:08:04.290
It's proven that the Quraysh are unqualified,

00:08:04.310 --> 00:08:07.160
unworthy of living up to the name of Ibrahim.

00:08:08.140 --> 00:08:11.080
Surah al-Kawthar is proof that Rasoolullah (صلى الله عليه وسلم)

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:13.450
is worthy of the legacy of Ibrahim.

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:15.870
We've given you Kawthar. What should you do?

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:20.960
What were the two things  Rasul (صلى الله عليه وسلم) was told to do in Surah al-Kawthar?

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:24.601
فَصَلِّ لِرَبِّكَ وَٱنۡحَرۡ

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:30.950
Pray and sacrifice. Oh, pray and sacrifice. Wait a second. Whose legacy is that?

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:34.850
Ibrahim (عليه السلام). You fulfill the legacy.

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:37.280
And then He says,

00:08:37.296 --> 00:08:39.100
إِنَّ شَانِئَكَ هُوَ ٱلۡأَبۡتَرُ

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:40.880
Your enemy will be discontinued.

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:44.420
Oh my God! Allah already started calling who an enemy?

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:45.760
Somebody's his enemy.

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:47.650
Somebody's the Prophet's enemy.

00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:50.810
And I know tafseer will tell us who the enemy is,

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:54.990
but in the text itself, it's a little ambiguous. "Your enemy will be discontinued."

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:56.170
So who is that enemy?

00:08:56.170 --> 00:09:00.549
Well, Allah just now mentioned that those people are unqualified.

00:09:00.559 --> 00:09:04.010
But the Prophet is
qualified. So they say, "Wait, wait, wait.

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:07.060
even if the Prophet is qualified, he's still Quraysh."

00:09:07.740 --> 00:09:09.060
"He's still one of us."

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:12.260
"We're all the same. We're all the same family."

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:16.490
Actually, you're no longer the same family. Don't tell them,

00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:19.770
[قُل يَا قَومِي], [قُل يَا قَبِيلَتِي], [قُل يَا قُرَيش]

00:09:19.790 --> 00:09:20.760
What is the next Surah?

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:23.510
قُلۡ یَـٰۤأَیُّهَا ٱلۡكَـٰفِرُونَ

00:09:23.530 --> 00:09:26.420
I'm gonna say that I have nothing to do with you people anymore.

00:09:26.430 --> 00:09:31.750
Yes, we were both the same blood. We're Banu
Hashim. We're from the Quraysh. We have lived here.

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:32.940
My ancestry is here.

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:34.984
But because of this [لَا إِِلَهَ إِلَّ الله]

00:09:35.004 --> 00:09:39.050
And because you have abandoned the legacy of our father Ibrahim, and I'm trying to

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:43.350
hold on to the legacy of our father Ibrahim, we are now two separate ways.

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:47.160
You are Kaafiroon. You are not my people anymore. I will not call you my people.

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:50.670
I will call you al-Kaafiroon, and I don't worship what you worship.

00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:53.470
And you don't worship what I worship. And you go your way, I go my way.

00:09:53.487 --> 00:09:55.820
لَكُمۡ دِینُكُمۡ وَلِیَ دِینِ

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:58.860
When you say that-- By the way, in the tribal world.

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:01.360
In tribal society.

00:10:02.140 --> 00:10:04.750
When you tell your tribe I have nothing to do with you.

00:10:05.140 --> 00:10:06.660
"You go your way. I go my way."

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:09.490
You know what that's considered? It's considered treason.

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:13.960
And once you declare that I have nothing to do with my tribe, that tribe becomes your

00:10:14.740 --> 00:10:15.360
enemy.

00:10:15.820 --> 00:10:16.410
In other words,

00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:17.720
قُلۡ یَـٰۤأَیُّهَا ٱلۡكَـٰفِرُونَ

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:20.220
is a declaration of war.

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:21.360
We have to understand,

00:10:21.370 --> 00:10:22.560
قُلۡ یَـٰۤأَیُّهَا ٱلۡكَـٰفِرُونَ

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:24.660
is a declaration of
war.

00:10:24.690 --> 00:10:29.630
Now, if there is a declaration of war, that
means from here on out there is a conflict.

00:10:29.630 --> 00:10:33.710
The physical conflict between the Prophet (صلى الله عليه وسلم) and who? And the Quraysh.

00:10:33.710 --> 00:10:37.100
His own people, who no longer get called his own people anymore.

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:39.790
If there is a conflict, then you have to--

00:10:39.790 --> 00:10:42.550
At the end of the day, in a conflict, somebody will win.

00:10:43.810 --> 00:10:45.810
Someone will win and someone will lose.

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:48.240
So what does Allah do in the next surah?

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:50.360
He let us know who's gonna win and who's gonna lose.

00:10:50.363 --> 00:10:54.400
إِذَا جَاۤءَ نَصۡرُ ٱللَّهِ وَٱلۡفَتۡحُ

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:57.690
وَرَأَیۡتَ ٱلنَّاسَ یَدۡخُلُونَ فِی دِینِ ٱللَّهِ أَفۡوَاجࣰا

00:10:57.690 --> 00:10:59.190
SubhaanAllah.

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:04.910
The war has been declared in al-Kafirun. The victor has been declared in

00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:07.410
إِذَا جَاۤءَ نَصۡرُ ٱللَّهِ وَٱلۡفَتۡحُ

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:11.350
But the promise of victory does not mean that the victory happens right away.

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:14.760
I'll give it to you in a visual way.

00:11:15.530 --> 00:11:17.660
You see the clouds, but it hasn't rained yet.

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:21.440
But before you know, even before you know it's going to rain,

00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:23.660
you can tell that it's going to rain because you're seeing the

00:11:24.140 --> 00:11:25.760
clouds, and you can feel in the wind.

00:11:26.140 --> 00:11:27.950
You can sense that rain is coming, right?

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:33.160
Now the Prophet has declared-- He's been told that victory is coming.

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:37.060
People are going to enter Islam in lots of numbers.

00:11:37.740 --> 00:11:39.450
And he was told this very early,

00:11:40.540 --> 00:11:42.390
and even though he was told this very early,

00:11:42.390 --> 00:11:45.820
it didn't look like Islam is gonna win very early.

00:11:45.830 --> 00:11:50.560
There were no indications that Islam will win actually because there were so few Sahaba

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:52.830
and the Quraysh were so powerful.

00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:55.350
Even elephants couldn't take them down.

00:11:57.040 --> 00:11:59.430
It didn't look like the Muslims are going to see people

00:11:59.430 --> 00:12:04.290
entering into Islam [أَفوَاجًا] multitudes, upon multitudes, upon multitudes.

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:05.560
Hard to imagine.

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:08.460
When you make a big promise of victory.

00:12:09.440 --> 00:12:10.850
When you make big promises.

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:15.000
Then it's important
to at least get some signs.

00:12:16.240 --> 00:12:16.860
Some hope.

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:19.760
This is an important concept.

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:22.450
So before I go to the next Surah, I want you to understand the concept.

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:25.260
Zakariya (عليه السلام)

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:28.160
is told that he's going to have a son.

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:29.850
Pretty big deal.

00:12:32.240 --> 00:12:37.860
It's a big deal. So he says, "Ya Allah, I
believe you, but can I have some sign?"

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:43.450
He says, "You won't speak to people for
three days." He gives him a sign.

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:50.120
Similarly, you have in the Quran, in this case, Allah (عز وجل)

00:12:50.150 --> 00:12:52.750
told Rasul (صلى الله عليه وسلم), you will take over all--

00:12:52.760 --> 00:12:54.360
The deen of Allah will be victorious.

00:12:56.140 --> 00:12:59.790
But unlike Zakariya, who went to Allah, and asked for a sign,

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:03.060
Allah does not wait for the Prophet to ask for a sign.

00:13:03.070 --> 00:13:07.732
Allah says: Listen. I know you don't think victory is easy. Let me show you. Okay,

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:09.351
you tell me who your worst enemy is.

00:13:09.422 --> 00:13:11.454
Okay, my worst enemy is Abu
Lahab.

00:13:11.777 --> 00:13:14.674
Okay, let Me make an example out of Abu Lahab for you.

00:13:14.740 --> 00:13:16.360
So you'll know that victory is coming.

00:13:17.740 --> 00:13:18.850
What's the next surah?

00:13:19.867 --> 00:13:21.550
تَبَّتۡ یَدَاۤ أَبِی لَهَبࣲ وَتَبَّ

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:24.440
It's not the destruction of all the enemies of Islam,

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:29.360
but the worst enemy of Islam is made an example out of, and he's destroyed.

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:34.460
Called out. Just so we know-- Just so the Prophet knows

00:13:34.460 --> 00:13:36.300
and the believers know that the promise of Allah

00:13:36.300 --> 00:13:41.330
that victory is coming is going to happen because Abu
Lahab was one of the most powerful people in Makkah.

00:13:41.340 --> 00:13:42.940
And also one of the worst enemies of Islam,

00:13:42.940 --> 00:13:44.610
if not the worst enemy of Islam.

00:13:44.610 --> 00:13:46.260
Arguably, the worst enemy of Islam.

00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:48.050
And Allah took care of him.

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:49.560
Now,

00:13:50.240 --> 00:13:51.750
Let's look at this sequence again.

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:54.710
The first two surahs were about the du'a of Ibrahim.

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:57.000
The next two surahs was who's qualified to fulfill

00:13:57.000 --> 00:13:59.720
the legacy and who's not qualified to fulfill the legacy.

00:13:59.730 --> 00:14:02.010
The next surah is the one who is qualified declares

00:14:02.010 --> 00:14:05.020
against-- war against the one who is not qualified.

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:08.230
Once the war is declared, the victor is declared in the next surah.

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:11.930
Once the victor is declared, here's a small token that victory is on its way.

00:14:11.930 --> 00:14:13.660
Abu Lahab, I'll take care of him for you.

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:16.560
Which means now their path to victory is clear.

00:14:17.220 --> 00:14:20.160
There are no obstacles left in our path to victory.

00:14:21.640 --> 00:14:24.540
When you go for a war for a long time-- And we we know that

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:27.970
really well in the United States. When you engage in war for a long time,

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:30.460
is it possible you forget what you are fighting in the first place?

00:14:31.440 --> 00:14:32.260
[laughs]

00:14:33.540 --> 00:14:35.250
You forget what you're fighting in the first place.

00:14:36.140 --> 00:14:37.250
What was the struggle for?

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:39.460
This is a real problem, by the way.

00:14:39.840 --> 00:14:41.470
This is a very real problem.

00:14:41.620 --> 00:14:46.050
There are people who are struggling to establish Islamic work, build a school,

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:50.870
do dawah work, build their organization. They've been at it for years.

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:51.420
But you know what?

00:14:51.420 --> 00:14:52.690
When you're at it for a long time,

00:14:52.690 --> 00:14:55.140
you sometimes forget why you were starting to begin with.

00:14:56.140 --> 00:14:59.390
There are students who want to-- when they first started studying Islam they said,

00:14:59.390 --> 00:15:01.960
"I just want to get close to Allah. I just want to pray.

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:05.330
And I want to understand what Allah is saying in every salah. That's all I want."

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:07.230
And they've been studying Islam for 10 years now,

00:15:07.230 --> 00:15:08.950
but they don't pay attention in salah anymore.

00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:12.250
That happens. You lose sight of why you started.

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:13.550
You forget.

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:16.360
When you started, it was very clear.

00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:20.790
Over time, the intention and
the motivation and the original

00:15:20.790 --> 00:15:23.250
inspiration that got you started becomes rusty.

00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:27.560
What does Allah do in this sequencing?

00:15:27.570 --> 00:15:31.450
Allah says: Well I have cleared the path of victory for you.

00:15:31.460 --> 00:15:36.340
But as the path of victory becomes clear, and you will be able to establish Allah's deen,

00:15:36.350 --> 00:15:38.750
I need you to remember what this struggle was about

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:42.260
to begin with. This struggle was about the legacy of which man?

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:47.760
Ibrahim (عليه السلام) and the legacy of
Ibrahim (عليه السلام) in one word, is Tawheed.

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:50.910
It is the Oneness of Allah. He is the father of monotheism.

00:15:51.320 --> 00:15:52.150
One God.

00:15:53.240 --> 00:15:55.750
The father of all monotheistic faiths, they call him.

00:15:56.740 --> 00:16:03.260
If that's the case, then we should be reminded of the constitution
of this faith after victory. What is the constitution of this faith?

00:16:03.840 --> 00:16:12.280
قُلۡ هُوَ ٱللَّهُ أَحَدٌ. ٱللَّهُ ٱلصَّمَدُ. لَمۡ یَلِدۡ وَلَمۡ یُولَدۡ. وَلَمۡ یَكُن لَّهُۥ كُفُوًا أَحَدُۢ

00:16:12.340 --> 00:16:13.490
That's what this deen is all about,

00:16:13.490 --> 00:16:17.160
at the end of the day. Just the oneness of God. Oneness of Allah. That's all it's about.

00:16:17.940 --> 00:16:21.860
You know? He has no son, He didn't give birth and He's not given birth.

00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:27.260
Now that that's established, Tawheed is
established, is another important question.

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:30.360
Did every prophet preach the same message of one God?

00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:31.750
Sure.

00:16:32.740 --> 00:16:36.800
Is it true that every prophet, after a generation or two of him being gone,

00:16:37.070 --> 00:16:39.250
things started going bad again?

00:16:40.840 --> 00:16:42.200
And after a few generations,

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:44.620
that same nation who was worshiping One God ended

00:16:44.620 --> 00:16:47.650
up falling into the clutches of shirk again.

00:16:48.140 --> 00:16:51.230
Did it happen over and over again in history? Sure.

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:55.870
Now you have gained victory and you have established the oneness of God.

00:16:55.880 --> 00:17:00.460
Is it possible that over time you will also fall trap to the, you know,

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:03.330
to the attempts - the attacks - of Shaytaan. Is it possible?

00:17:03.340 --> 00:17:06.950
Is it possible you will lose your Tawhid? Is it possible? Sure.

00:17:07.740 --> 00:17:12.410
And that oneness of Iman, the oneness of God, the Tawheed of Allah, the iman in Allah,

00:17:12.410 --> 00:17:16.119
the [لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّ الله] that lives inside the people's hearts.

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:17.660
It has to be protected.

00:17:17.670 --> 00:17:18.869
But to protect it,

00:17:18.880 --> 00:17:21.130
you have to protect it from the attacks that come

00:17:21.130 --> 00:17:25.050
from the outside and the
attacks that come from the inside.

00:17:25.060 --> 00:17:28.710
The attacks that come from the outside should be protected against.

00:17:28.710 --> 00:17:32.720
So Allah sent us the protection from the outside by revealing,

00:17:32.740 --> 00:17:35.041
قُلۡ أَعُوذُ بِرَبِّ ٱلۡفَلَقِ

00:17:36.440 --> 00:17:37.850
مِن شَرِّ مَا خَلَقَ

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:40.150
وَمِن شَرِّ غَاسِقٍ إِذَا وَقَبَ

00:17:40.507 --> 00:17:42.310
وَمِن شَرِّ ٱلنَّفَّـٰثَـٰتِ فِی ٱلۡعُقَدِ

00:17:42.440 --> 00:17:44.720
وَمِن شَرِّ حَاسِدٍ إِذَا حَسَدَ

00:17:44.780 --> 00:17:45.950
These are attacks from the

00:17:46.440 --> 00:17:48.360
outside that can ruin your faith.

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:50.660
What kind of attacks are left?

00:17:51.940 --> 00:17:54.360
The attacks on the inside. Well, what's last surah?

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:57.070
قُلۡ أَعُوذُ بِرَبِّ ٱلنَّاسِ

00:17:57.070 --> 00:17:58.380
مَلِكِ ٱلنَّاسِ

00:17:58.380 --> 00:17:59.520
إِلَـٰهِ ٱلنَّاسِ

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:04.760
مِن شَرِّ ٱلۡوَسۡوَاسِ ٱلۡخَنَّاسِ ٱلَّذِی یُوَسۡوِسُ فِی صُدُورِ ٱلنَّاسِ

00:18:04.820 --> 00:18:09.490
We ask Allah to protect us from the whispers of those-- of the Shayaateen, the devils,

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:12.170
who whisper inside the chests of people.

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:13.520
Beautiful language.

00:18:13.520 --> 00:18:16.550
Allah says they whisper inside the chests of the people,

00:18:16.640 --> 00:18:19.670
He does not say they whisper inside the hearts of the people.

00:18:20.340 --> 00:18:21.560
Beautiful language.

00:18:21.940 --> 00:18:25.150
What's the difference between saying the devils have access to the chests,

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:27.990
as opposed to saying the devils have access to the heart?

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:33.160
The chest is a place. The heart is a thing. The heart is inside the chest.

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:37.130
It is as though they have-- Imagine there's a castle,

00:18:37.140 --> 00:18:39.170
but there's a wall outside the castle.

00:18:39.740 --> 00:18:40.960
So there's a perimeter.

00:18:41.410 --> 00:18:42.980
The shayaateen are given access

00:18:43.130 --> 00:18:46.560
inside the gate, but they still don't have access to the castle itself.

00:18:47.090 --> 00:18:50.290
Allah did not give the devils access to our heart's.

00:18:50.540 --> 00:18:54.060
The only one who can
open the door for them is us.

00:18:54.640 --> 00:18:55.513
That's why He didn't say,

00:18:55.524 --> 00:18:57.444
ٱلَّذِی یُوَسۡوِسُ فِی قُلُوبِ ٱلنَّاسِ

00:18:57.454 --> 00:19:00.204
He said,
ٱلَّذِی یُوَسۡوِسُ فِی صُدُورِ ٱلنَّاسِ

00:19:00.224 --> 00:19:01.450
مِنَ ٱلۡجِنَّةِ وَٱلنَّاسِ

00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:04.790
Everything is connected to everything else,

00:19:04.790 --> 00:19:07.160
and it goes together to make a comprehensive argument.

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:11.290
Everything flows together and makes a comprehensive argument.

00:19:11.300 --> 00:19:16.270
This is the structure of-- or the organization of surahs in the Quran.

00:19:16.640 --> 00:19:19.500
There are for example-- There are many examples of this. One

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:22.160
surah will talk about, you know, um,

00:19:22.740 --> 00:19:26.460
it's awesome, one surah will talk about people burning in hellfire.

00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:32.260
And they're saying, "Hey, we're burning. But
where are those guys that we thought were losers?"

00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:33.560
"We don't see them here."

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:34.860
Who are they talking about?

00:19:35.840 --> 00:19:36.670
The Muslims.

00:19:37.340 --> 00:19:38.360
We don't see them burning.

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:41.620
"We used to think they were pathetic."

00:19:41.630 --> 00:19:42.990
"How come they're not here with us?"

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:44.850
But where are they?

00:19:45.740 --> 00:19:48.800
In Jannah. The next surah the conversation is reversed.

00:19:48.810 --> 00:19:50.160
There are a bunch of people in heaven.

00:19:50.170 --> 00:19:53.660
There are a bunch of people in paradise, and one of them says, "Hey, where's my friend?"

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:55.050
"Where'd he go?"

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:56.860
"We used to hang out together."

00:19:57.400 --> 00:19:58.560
And guess what he finds out.

00:19:59.440 --> 00:20:01.170
That friend of his that is missing is where?

00:20:02.040 --> 00:20:02.670
In Jahannam.

00:20:03.240 --> 00:20:05.760
So Allah paints one picture in one surah,

00:20:05.770 --> 00:20:07.860
then He paints the opposite picture in the next surah.

00:20:09.840 --> 00:20:11.970
He does this all over the Quran.

00:20:11.980 --> 00:20:14.920
Things are tied together and connected together. In other words,

00:20:14.920 --> 00:20:18.730
the organization of the Quran and the sequencing of the Quran,

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:22.000
it does not make itself obvious to you when you're reading it.

00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:26.150
Which is why when you've tried to read the
Quran before in translation from one to the--

00:20:26.150 --> 00:20:29.270
One chapter-- See I'm saying chapter because you thought it was a chapter--

00:20:29.440 --> 00:20:31.450
One chapter to the next to the next to the next.

00:20:31.540 --> 00:20:33.270
You weren't able to see the connection.

00:20:34.340 --> 00:20:38.170
You're not able to see the connection. It takes work to discover this order.

00:20:38.540 --> 00:20:41.190
And the more work you put in, the more beautiful it gets.

00:20:42.140 --> 00:20:43.550
The more remarkable it gets.

00:20:44.440 --> 00:20:47.230
So on that note, I've tried to
talk to you a little bit about the

00:20:47.230 --> 00:20:51.150
relationship between different parts or different surahs of the Quran.

00:20:51.160 --> 00:20:52.960
But what I want to talk to you about now

00:20:53.840 --> 00:20:55.850
is actually what happens inside a surah.

00:20:57.440 --> 00:20:59.170
What about within a surah itself?

00:21:00.200 --> 00:21:03.390
This is Section 9. It's on page 22 of your notes.

00:21:05.040 --> 00:21:06.980
This is the story of Yusuf (عليه السلام).

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:09.450
There's lots to talk about here, but I'll make it brief.

00:21:10.140 --> 00:21:11.960
I feel like I'm running out of time already.

00:21:12.640 --> 00:21:13.450
I really do.

00:21:14.640 --> 00:21:16.460
Too many great things to talk to you about.

00:21:18.240 --> 00:21:21.860
I will have you read this with me out loud. What is A?

00:21:22.776 --> 00:21:23.611
[crowd responds]

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:24.170
Good.

00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:26.391
I need louder next time. What is B?

00:21:26.761 --> 00:21:28.860
[crowd responds]

00:21:29.040 --> 00:21:29.850
C?

00:21:30.091 --> 00:21:32.711
[crowd responds]

00:21:33.040 --> 00:21:34.450
Okay, D?

00:21:34.450 --> 00:21:36.950
[crowd responds]

00:21:37.371 --> 00:21:38.170
E?

00:21:38.170 --> 00:21:39.730
[crowd responds]

00:21:39.740 --> 00:21:40.360
F?

00:21:40.360 --> 00:21:41.530
[crowd responds]

00:21:41.540 --> 00:21:42.530
Okay. Okay. Stop now.

00:21:43.640 --> 00:21:44.560
Good reading. Good job.

00:21:45.940 --> 00:21:47.950
Okay. Read K for me.

00:21:48.340 --> 00:21:49.890
[crowd responds]

00:21:49.940 --> 00:21:52.850
Do you understand what I'm doing here? It's in the order of the surah.

00:21:53.440 --> 00:21:55.130
Okay. Read K for me again.

00:21:55.490 --> 00:21:57.480
[crowd responds]

00:21:57.540 --> 00:21:59.320
Okay. Read A for me again.

00:21:59.320 --> 00:22:00.720
[crowd responds]

00:22:00.740 --> 00:22:01.550
Oh,

00:22:02.740 --> 00:22:04.060
Read B for me.

00:22:04.604 --> 00:22:07.104
[crowd responds]

00:22:07.640 --> 00:22:08.770
Read J.

00:22:08.770 --> 00:22:11.080
[crowd responds]

00:22:11.140 --> 00:22:11.670
Whoa.

00:22:12.540 --> 00:22:14.060
Okay, okay, okay. Let's go back. Let's go back.

00:22:14.940 --> 00:22:18.690
Read, "Minister's wife's attempt to seduce Yusuf." That's C.

00:22:18.690 --> 00:22:20.060
What am I going to make you read now?

00:22:20.840 --> 00:22:21.800
Read I.

00:22:22.210 --> 00:22:25.820
[crowd responds]

00:22:25.940 --> 00:22:27.260
Whoa.

00:22:27.740 --> 00:22:28.670
What!?

00:22:30.340 --> 00:22:31.360
D.

00:22:31.760 --> 00:22:33.680
[crowd responds]

00:22:33.730 --> 00:22:37.390
C and D are together. C and D are together and then I is responding to them.

00:22:37.390 --> 00:22:38.560
But let's go back again.

00:22:39.540 --> 00:22:40.350
E.

00:22:40.563 --> 00:22:42.001
[crowd responds]

00:22:42.040 --> 00:22:42.670
Mmhmm.

00:22:43.540 --> 00:22:44.560
Yusuf's in prison.

00:22:45.840 --> 00:22:46.350
H.

00:22:46.898 --> 00:22:48.801
[crowd responds]

00:22:48.840 --> 00:22:52.260
Uhh, okay, okay, okay. This one gotta be off-- "The king's dream..."

00:22:53.470 --> 00:22:56.820
[crowd finishes sentence]

00:22:56.840 --> 00:22:57.860
Oh, my God.

00:22:59.940 --> 00:23:01.350
You see how the surah is organised?

00:23:03.440 --> 00:23:06.530
Every problem discussed in the first half of Surah

00:23:06.530 --> 00:23:10.060
Yusuf is solved in reverse order in the second half of Surah Yusuf.

00:23:11.840 --> 00:23:13.060
It's a perfect symmetry.

00:23:14.740 --> 00:23:18.550
When I was in literature class in college, in the first year of college,

00:23:20.140 --> 00:23:23.700
we were given a homework assignment to compare the story of Joseph

00:23:23.700 --> 00:23:26.860
in the Bible to the story of Joseph in the "Koran".

00:23:29.540 --> 00:23:33.760
At the time, I was not a student of the Arabic language, nor of Islam.

00:23:33.760 --> 00:23:36.770
As a matter of fact, at the time I wasn't even interested in religion.

00:23:38.540 --> 00:23:41.320
And I thought it was a good opportunity to read something from the Quran.

00:23:41.330 --> 00:23:44.660
So in our textbook they had the two excerpts from the two

00:23:45.040 --> 00:23:47.950
accounts next to one another, and I read them quickly.

00:23:48.840 --> 00:23:49.950
And at the time I thought,

00:23:51.040 --> 00:23:53.310
"I don't know. The Bible just has more details, I guess."

00:23:54.340 --> 00:23:55.270
I didn't know what to write.

00:23:56.940 --> 00:24:04.010
And my professor also said, "Well, the Koran's version
is pretty much a brief account of the biblical version."

00:24:04.020 --> 00:24:05.850
"Nothing really much to it there."

00:24:07.140 --> 00:24:11.260
Well, Professor,
I must say,

00:24:11.840 --> 00:24:14.320
I didn't have to actually learn Arabic to know

00:24:14.320 --> 00:24:17.960
that there's an incredible literary symmetry in this surah.

00:24:18.640 --> 00:24:20.050
From beginning to the end.

00:24:21.040 --> 00:24:23.160
I didn't have to know, you know, anything else,

00:24:23.160 --> 00:24:25.910
but just the surah itself, just a little bit about it.

00:24:25.920 --> 00:24:30.360
And, you know, for me to understand that Allah (عز وجل) revealed this in perfect order.

00:24:30.370 --> 00:24:33.060
Now imagine,
to do this

00:24:33.190 --> 00:24:35.890
as an oral tradition with no edits.

00:24:35.950 --> 00:24:39.760
First time, he's just reciting it and it just comes out like this.

00:24:41.140 --> 00:24:45.340
Which is why, at the end of it, you know what Allah says? At the end of Surah Yusuf?

00:24:45.350 --> 00:24:45.890
He says,

00:24:45.890 --> 00:24:47.350
مَا كَانَ حَدِیثࣰا یُفۡتَرَىٰ

00:24:47.740 --> 00:24:49.060
It's not speech that's made up.

00:24:49.940 --> 00:24:51.050
You can't make this stuff up

00:24:52.340 --> 00:24:54.621
It's literally what Allah says at the end of Surah Yusuf.

00:24:55.840 --> 00:24:59.230
I've previously spoken to you about the symmetry or the order

00:24:59.230 --> 00:25:02.240
and the structure inside Surah al-Rahman and its relationship with

00:25:02.256 --> 00:25:04.660
Surah al-Waqi'ah. As a brief reminder to you,

00:25:05.540 --> 00:25:09.560
Surah al-Rahman has five sections. Surah al-Waqi'ah has five sections.

00:25:10.240 --> 00:25:13.300
Surah al-Rahman has five. Surah al-Waqi'ah has five.

00:25:13.310 --> 00:25:16.170
Surah al-Rahman - the first section is the greatness of the Quran.

00:25:16.840 --> 00:25:18.780
First section is about the greatness of the Quran.

00:25:18.780 --> 00:25:22.200
ٱلرَّحۡمَـٰنُ. عَلَّمَ ٱلۡقُرۡءَانَ. خَلَقَ ٱلۡإِنسَـٰنَ. عَلَّمَهُ ٱلۡبَیَانَ

00:25:22.240 --> 00:25:25.330
Surah al-Waqi'ah - the last section is about the greatness of the Quran.

00:25:25.330 --> 00:25:30.360
فَلَاۤ أُقۡسِمُ بِمَوَ ٰ⁠قِعِ ٱلنُّجُومِ. وَإِنَّهُۥ لَقَسَمࣱ لَّوۡ تَعۡلَمُونَ عَظِیمٌ

00:25:30.440 --> 00:25:35.120
So in Surah al-Rahman, it was section one, and in Surah al-Waqi'ah - the next surah - it is section

00:25:35.140 --> 00:25:39.440
five. In Surah al-Rahman, section two is about the creations of Allah.

00:25:39.462 --> 00:25:42.460
In Surah al-Waqi'ah, section four is about the creations of Allah.

00:25:44.240 --> 00:25:48.770
In Surah al-Rahman, section three is about health, Judgment Day, and Hellfire.

00:25:49.740 --> 00:25:53.220
Section three is about Judgment Day and Hellfire. In Surah al-Waqi'ah

00:25:53.220 --> 00:25:55.350
section three is about Judgment Day and hellfire.

00:25:56.840 --> 00:26:01.060
In Surah al-Rahman, section four is about the first level of Jannah.

00:26:01.640 --> 00:26:04.334
First two levels of jannah or two kinds of jannah

00:26:04.340 --> 00:26:06.910
that are at the-- economy class Jannah basically.

00:26:08.040 --> 00:26:08.460
Okay?

00:26:09.440 --> 00:26:12.460
In Surah al-Waqi'ah, section-- What section should I talk about?

00:26:13.340 --> 00:26:16.530
Section two. Because we're talking about section four from Rahman.

00:26:16.540 --> 00:26:17.850
So now here,

00:26:17.850 --> 00:26:21.860
section two is about the People of the Right Hand. Where do People of the Right Hand go?

00:26:22.940 --> 00:26:23.660
Enter jannah.

00:26:24.540 --> 00:26:28.630
The final section of Surah al-Rahman is an elite, elaborate,

00:26:28.640 --> 00:26:31.350
extra beautiful place in Jannah.

00:26:32.440 --> 00:26:36.370
Section one of Surah al-Waqiah, Allah describes the people that are called

00:26:36.380 --> 00:26:39.592
وَٱلسَّـٰبِقُونَ ٱلسَّـٰبِقُونَ، أُو۟لَـٰۤىِٕكَ ٱلۡمُقَرَّبُونَ

00:26:39.600 --> 00:26:43.700
The first and the foremost. Those are the ones that are brought close to Allah.

00:26:44.140 --> 00:26:46.960
The first and the foremost. Shouldn't they get the elite place in Jannah?

00:26:47.940 --> 00:26:48.450
Mhm.

00:26:49.140 --> 00:26:52.550
Five sections of al-Rahman, then reversed in five sections of al-Waq'iah.

00:26:52.550 --> 00:26:53.550
Mirroring each other.

00:26:54.540 --> 00:26:55.860
Just completely mirroring each other.

00:26:57.540 --> 00:27:00.660
There's remarkable
connectivity.

00:27:01.340 --> 00:27:05.060
Within a surah of the Quran and between surahs of the Quran.

00:27:05.940 --> 00:27:08.090
Within the surah and between the surahs.

00:27:08.540 --> 00:27:09.950
It's an incredible study.

00:27:10.540 --> 00:27:14.170
And what it does is it completely changes the way you view

00:27:14.820 --> 00:27:16.060
the Quran as a book.

00:27:17.140 --> 00:27:21.020
Because for a lot of us, including myself, when I was first introduced to the Quran

00:27:21.030 --> 00:27:26.838
it actually didn't feel like a book. It actually felt like a set of isolated aayaat.

00:27:27.540 --> 00:27:31.490
Like, you kind of study one aayah at a time or you learn one lesson at a time,

00:27:31.500 --> 00:27:34.460
but you don't technically look at it as something connected

00:27:34.840 --> 00:27:38.020
and something that flows from one thing to the next to the next.

00:27:38.030 --> 00:27:41.560
By the way, Quran, one of the meetings of [قَرَنَ] is "to flow".

00:27:42.540 --> 00:27:45.340
Some argue that the origin of Quran is not [قَرَاَ], it's [قَرَنَ],

00:27:45.350 --> 00:27:48.860
which actually means "to flow", like the entire Quran flows.

00:27:49.840 --> 00:27:54.410
Make du'a that I am able to finish this
project with the help of my colleagues.

00:27:54.410 --> 00:27:57.720
Every year I give myself a new project in Quran studies,

00:27:57.720 --> 00:28:01.060
so this year's project, inshaaAllah, is to write and then

00:28:01.060 --> 00:28:05.360
eventually present a comprehensive introduction to every surah of the Quran.

00:28:05.940 --> 00:28:09.770
InshaaAllah Ta'aalaa. The intent is to-- what I've been saying "comprehensive introduction"

00:28:09.770 --> 00:28:12.960
not just what are the subjects inside the surah and when it was revealed,

00:28:12.960 --> 00:28:16.090
but how is this surah organized from beginning to end?

00:28:16.090 --> 00:28:19.690
How does everything connect with everything else? What is the layout of the surah?

00:28:19.690 --> 00:28:22.170
A kind of a map of the surah, like we did with Surah Yusuf.

00:28:22.940 --> 00:28:26.770
Kind of like that. Exploring the beauty in the map of every Sura.

00:28:27.540 --> 00:28:29.810
You know? It's going to be quite an adventure, I think,

00:28:29.810 --> 00:28:31.920
InshaaAllah Ta'aalaa, just to engage in that study.

00:28:31.930 --> 00:28:34.350
So pray that Allah gives success in that study, bi-idhnillah.

00:28:34.840 --> 00:28:38.970
OK. On this note, I do want to highlight at least one-- since we're on the case of

00:28:38.970 --> 00:28:42.210
Surah Yusuf, I just wanna give one example of

00:28:42.220 --> 00:28:45.300
things that are talked about in Surah Yusuf. Things are balanced, right?

00:28:45.310 --> 00:28:47.590
One thing is mentioned here, is balanced on the other side.

00:28:47.600 --> 00:28:50.230
And so there is actually an interesting balance

00:28:50.230 --> 00:28:53.110
even within the characters that are mentioned in Surah Yusuf.

00:28:53.110 --> 00:28:57.060
So I'll just highlight one aspect of that. I'll talk about Yusuf (عليه السلام) himself.

00:28:57.340 --> 00:28:59.520
And two opposite sides of his personality.

00:28:59.530 --> 00:29:03.630
On the one side, there is his humility and on the other side of humility

00:29:03.630 --> 00:29:04.960
there is his confidence.

00:29:05.740 --> 00:29:08.720
So we'll we'll contrast those two qualities of Yusuf (عليه السلام).

00:29:08.970 --> 00:29:11.630
His humility versus his confidence.

00:29:13.040 --> 00:29:15.000
You know, kids, they have funny ways of talking.

00:29:16.540 --> 00:29:19.080
When kids are really excited or nervous. When kids are nervous

00:29:19.540 --> 00:29:21.650
they come to you and they say, uh, you know-

00:29:21.650 --> 00:29:25.770
like my my son will come in from the playground, his pants like his-- over here

00:29:25.760 --> 00:29:29.850
that has got dirt on them. His hands are dirty. "What happened? What happened Imad?"

00:29:29.870 --> 00:29:38.050
"Um, um, I was playing. Uh, I was playing, uh, and then I was playing. And then, um,

00:29:38.540 --> 00:29:41.660
uh, we were on the swings and I was playing."

00:29:44.640 --> 00:29:46.050
When kids are nervous, what do they do?

00:29:47.240 --> 00:29:48.460
They repeat themselves.

00:29:49.340 --> 00:29:51.050
They're not able to finish a sentence.

00:29:52.140 --> 00:29:52.650
They're not--

00:29:52.660 --> 00:29:55.170
They don't have enough confidence to be able to finish the whole thought.

00:29:55.540 --> 00:29:59.020
You have to, "It's okay. It's okay Imad. You can tell me. You're not in trouble."

00:29:59.030 --> 00:30:00.960
"I'm not gonna be mad. It's okay."

00:30:01.440 --> 00:30:04.670
There's a kind of fear and a kind of nervousness. A kind of humility, even.

00:30:05.240 --> 00:30:07.270
and they're not able to express themselves. You understand?

00:30:07.740 --> 00:30:10.540
Yusuf (عليه السلام) is a child. He sees a dream.

00:30:10.550 --> 00:30:15.040
He sees a dream in which 11 stars, and the sun, and the moon are doing sajdah to him.

00:30:15.050 --> 00:30:18.541
He comes to his dad and he says [إِنِيْ رَاَيْتُ]

00:30:18.561 --> 00:30:23.810
[يَا أَبَتِي] "Dad, I love you." [إِنِّي رَاَيْتُ] "No doubt about it. I did see it. Really I did."

00:30:23.810 --> 00:30:27.610
"I did". The fact that he said [إِنِّي] he almost expects that it's so crazy,

00:30:27.610 --> 00:30:28.560
Dad won't believe me.

00:30:30.340 --> 00:30:31.660
So he said [إِنِّي رَاَيْتُ].

00:30:32.160 --> 00:30:32.785
He said,

00:30:32.785 --> 00:30:35.285
إِنِّی رَأَیۡتُ أَحَدَ عَشَرَ كَوۡكَبࣰا وَٱلشَّمۡسَ وَٱلۡقَمَرَ

00:30:35.300 --> 00:30:37.975
"No doubt, Dad. I'm telling you. Really, I did see it, Dad."

00:30:37.980 --> 00:30:40.560
"I saw 11 stars, the sun, and the moon..."

00:30:42.410 --> 00:30:43.170
And he stopped.

00:30:44.140 --> 00:30:45.360
He stops talking.

00:30:46.140 --> 00:30:47.760
He doesn't continue.

00:30:48.240 --> 00:30:51.710
It's almost as though he has to be, "It's okay. You can tell me, you can tell me."

00:30:51.720 --> 00:30:54.670
And he had to start over again and said-- Because you know,

00:30:54.670 --> 00:30:57.780
when he got to 11 stars and the sun and the moon, what were the sun and the moon doing?

00:30:57.790 --> 00:30:58.460
What were they doing?

00:30:59.440 --> 00:31:00.200
They were prostrating.

00:31:00.200 --> 00:31:03.470
That part is the part that bothered him because he's so humble.

00:31:03.480 --> 00:31:05.630
And for him to be-- because, you know,

00:31:05.630 --> 00:31:07.960
prostrating to someone is to consider them great.

00:31:08.440 --> 00:31:11.550
It's a way of kind of like praising myself. "Things were doing sajdah to me.

00:31:11.560 --> 00:31:13.060
By the way, Dad, right here."

00:31:13.840 --> 00:31:18.460
"This is where I sat, even the sun
and the moon, and the 11 stars."

00:31:19.140 --> 00:31:19.670
You know?

00:31:20.840 --> 00:31:25.440
But he's so humble that the idea of them doing sajdah to him bothers him so much.

00:31:25.450 --> 00:31:29.590
He said "I saw 11 stars." He says, "I
saw the sun." He says, "I saw the moon."

00:31:29.600 --> 00:31:32.660
But when it came to the part about sajdah he couldn't continue.

00:31:33.640 --> 00:31:35.060
So he had to start over again.

00:31:35.280 --> 00:31:35.780
And he says,

00:31:35.800 --> 00:31:37.220
رَأَیۡتُهُمۡ لِی سَـٰجِدِینَ

00:31:37.220 --> 00:31:40.900
"I saw them." Wait, he already said "I saw" in the beginning,

00:31:40.940 --> 00:31:43.820
He already said that in the beginning. He had to say it again.

00:31:43.840 --> 00:31:45.670
رَأَیۡتُهُمۡ لِی سَـٰجِدِینَ

00:31:46.740 --> 00:31:50.930
And it's interesting that in the language of the aayah he uses the living pronouns,

00:31:50.940 --> 00:31:53.850
which suggests that he already had interpreted the dream.

00:31:54.240 --> 00:31:56.594
He doesn't say [رَأَيتُهَا] or [رَأَيتُهُنَّ],

00:31:56.614 --> 00:31:58.970
He said,
رَأَیۡتُهُمۡ لِی سَـٰجِدِینَ

00:31:58.970 --> 00:32:00.920
which means he used [اَلعَاقِل].

00:32:00.940 --> 00:32:05.080
Right? Which linguistically what that means is he actually, by the way he spoke

00:32:05.090 --> 00:32:06.670
you could tell he already figured it out.

00:32:07.340 --> 00:32:09.950
That it was his 11 brothers and his mom and his dad,

00:32:10.940 --> 00:32:12.560
which is what bothered him even more.

00:32:13.340 --> 00:32:17.880
And his dad's really smart. He picked up on the fact that this kid is really sharp.

00:32:17.890 --> 00:32:21.080
He figured out a dream, and he's this young and he can already figure it out.

00:32:21.090 --> 00:32:24.860
And he's telling me. And the way he told me the
dream, I could tell he already figured it out, too.

00:32:25.440 --> 00:32:27.310
Which is why his dad was really impressed with him and

00:32:27.310 --> 00:32:29.890
complimented him with a bunch of compliments in the next aayah.

00:32:29.900 --> 00:32:33.880
But this-- I wanted to highlight this portion, at least, for a couple of reasons.

00:32:33.880 --> 00:32:38.060
The first reason is it illustrates
the humility of Yusuf (عليه السلام).

00:32:39.140 --> 00:32:41.800
It also illustrates-- How many dads in the audience? Fathers?

00:32:42.410 --> 00:32:45.770
Any fathers? Okay, this is for you and me. I'm a father too.

00:32:46.340 --> 00:32:47.270
This is for you and me.

00:32:49.340 --> 00:32:50.860
Your sons and your daughters.

00:32:52.140 --> 00:32:54.170
Are they so comfortable with you?

00:32:55.040 --> 00:32:58.060
Are they so at ease with you as a father

00:32:59.010 --> 00:33:00.170
that they see a dream

00:33:00.840 --> 00:33:02.760
and the first person they want to tell is you?

00:33:03.840 --> 00:33:04.340
[snickers]

00:33:08.940 --> 00:33:10.460
"Dad, I saw a dream."

00:33:11.540 --> 00:33:12.860
"Go tell your mother, boy."

00:33:13.240 --> 00:33:14.760
[laughs]

00:33:18.940 --> 00:33:21.890
Actually, most of the time, our kids are talking to us, we're not even listening.

00:33:23.240 --> 00:33:25.550
Especially if it's our girls talking because they talk a lot.

00:33:27.240 --> 00:33:29.400
"Dad, you know what happened at school today? I was writing a book,

00:33:29.400 --> 00:33:31.460
I was reading a book, and then my friend came and said,

00:33:31.460 --> 00:33:32.210
'Why are you reading this book?'

00:33:32.230 --> 00:33:33.230
I said, 'Because it's in my homework

00:33:33.230 --> 00:33:35.850
I wanted to do homework in the library instead of going home and doing the homework.'

00:33:37.340 --> 00:33:39.970
But then we started talking. We started playing tic tac toe. She won the first one.

00:33:39.970 --> 00:33:42.560
I won the second one. I won the third one. She won the fourth one. It was really bad."

00:33:44.240 --> 00:33:47.450
What are you doing in the meantime? "Mmhm. That's great.

00:33:48.040 --> 00:33:50.860
Wow, that's wonderful." You're not listening.

00:33:52.140 --> 00:33:55.560
And the girl knows you're not listening. So she says, "Dad, can I have $5?"
"Mmmhm,

00:33:55.940 --> 00:33:56.270
Yep."

00:33:56.740 --> 00:34:00.960
"Can I tell Mama you said give them $5?"
"Mmmhm. Yes."

00:34:01.340 --> 00:34:05.060
So she goes over to the mother. "Abba said you need to give me $5."

00:34:06.440 --> 00:34:07.670
Then the mother calls you.

00:34:09.139 --> 00:34:12.860
"Did you say you?"
"Mmmhm". Because you're not listening to the wife either.

00:34:13.840 --> 00:34:15.060
[laughs]

00:34:15.840 --> 00:34:18.170
And that's how your girl makes money.

00:34:18.540 --> 00:34:19.670
[laughs]

00:34:21.139 --> 00:34:26.100
The aayah is teaching parents that they have to live up to the legacy of Ya'qoob (عليه السلام),

00:34:26.130 --> 00:34:28.890
and be attentive listeners to their children.

00:34:29.940 --> 00:34:33.659
As a matter of fact, Yusuf (عليه السلام) was not raised by

00:34:34.139 --> 00:34:38.350
a father. He was raised, just in his early childhood by that father.

00:34:38.520 --> 00:34:41.260
Pretty much the rest of his young years were raised

00:34:41.429 --> 00:34:44.760
as a servant living in another house without a father figure.

00:34:45.239 --> 00:34:46.389
He had no father figure.

00:34:46.530 --> 00:34:47.120
And, you know,

00:34:47.120 --> 00:34:49.850
a lot of times in modern society they say that young

00:34:49.850 --> 00:34:52.639
people resort to crime because they have no father figure,

00:34:52.679 --> 00:34:55.150
single family homes, mothers raising the son,

00:34:55.170 --> 00:34:57.010
the son goes out and has no father figure.

00:34:57.010 --> 00:35:02.160
So he gets involved in crimes, gangs, drugs, alcohol, partying, you name it.

00:35:02.240 --> 00:35:04.590
And then they say, "Well, because he had no dad in the home."

00:35:04.590 --> 00:35:05.370
There's no dad in the home.

00:35:05.370 --> 00:35:07.850
And that's why there's actually a judge in Brooklyn in New York

00:35:08.040 --> 00:35:10.460
who wrote a book on this because he was a juvenile judge.

00:35:10.460 --> 00:35:15.280
He was a judge for 35 years, and he sent like 18-19 year-olds to jail.

00:35:15.290 --> 00:35:18.700
And his conclusion at the end of 35 years is when there is no father figure,

00:35:18.700 --> 00:35:20.250
you will get young people turning to crime.

00:35:21.740 --> 00:35:23.100
That was his conclusion.

00:35:23.290 --> 00:35:26.860
And I can almost guarantee you that is not just a conclusion for Brooklyn, New York.

00:35:27.840 --> 00:35:30.060
I can almost guarantee you that's a conclusion for the entire world.

00:35:31.740 --> 00:35:34.329
But the problem here is Yusuf (عليه السلام)

00:35:34.369 --> 00:35:38.400
only received fatherly counsel at a very, very young age.

00:35:38.410 --> 00:35:41.050
And then the father was no more. He wasn't available.

00:35:41.060 --> 00:35:43.370
What we're learning, then, is even fatherly

00:35:43.370 --> 00:35:49.470
counsel at a very young age can be so powerful that it can help you survive teen years.

00:35:50.140 --> 00:35:52.590
Because a young man without a father and a mother

00:35:53.440 --> 00:35:57.160
in a house and a lady is saying, "Come on, don't you want to have some fun?"

00:35:58.340 --> 00:35:59.470
And he backs away.

00:36:00.530 --> 00:36:01.550
He backs away.

00:36:03.330 --> 00:36:06.550
The only tarbiya he had was from his dad. That's all.

00:36:07.730 --> 00:36:09.650
And the fact that he's thrown in prison.

00:36:10.330 --> 00:36:12.800
And when he talks to prisoners, he says, "By the way,

00:36:12.920 --> 00:36:14.550
I follow the religion of my dad."

00:36:15.830 --> 00:36:17.840
He talked about his dad in prison.

00:36:18.730 --> 00:36:21.620
Where did he learn about
his dad? When he was little.

00:36:21.630 --> 00:36:25.350
What we're learning in the idea is the value and the power of early education.

00:36:26.620 --> 00:36:28.660
Especially when it comes from which figure?

00:36:29.430 --> 00:36:29.950
The father.

00:36:30.130 --> 00:36:32.550
Anyway, this was a little bit about the humility of

00:36:33.030 --> 00:36:33.960
Yusuf (عليه السلام).

00:36:34.530 --> 00:36:37.550
In Islam we celebrate humility. "We're supposed to be humble brother."

00:36:38.430 --> 00:36:39.240
"Don't praise anyone."

00:36:41.130 --> 00:36:42.450
"Don't let anybody become arrogant."

00:36:42.830 --> 00:36:45.460
This is why husbands never praise their wives, right? Right?

00:36:45.470 --> 00:36:47.660
"We're trying to make them humble. We're doing them a favor."

00:36:48.430 --> 00:36:49.350
"We're helping them out."

00:36:50.330 --> 00:36:52.750
They help us out too. They help us a lot, don't they?

00:36:53.630 --> 00:36:55.290
Like some of you have blood pressure problems.

00:36:55.290 --> 00:36:57.530
Your wife-- or you have low blood pressure,

00:36:57.530 --> 00:36:59.620
so your wife helps you by keeping your blood pressure high?

00:37:00.240 --> 00:37:01.000
[laughs]

00:37:02.730 --> 00:37:05.460
This is an act of love. You have to understand, it's an act of love.

00:37:06.530 --> 00:37:10.250
Like your wife will come to you, "What kind of sandwich you want? Chicken or turkey?"

00:37:11.630 --> 00:37:14.240
You'll say "Chicken."
She says, "We don't have any chicken."

00:37:20.810 --> 00:37:23.740
And it'll raise your blood pressure. She's keeping you healthy.

00:37:24.230 --> 00:37:27.050
This is why she's doing this. But anyway, [laughs]

00:37:27.930 --> 00:37:30.390
Now let's talk a little-- So on the one hand, there is humility.

00:37:30.390 --> 00:37:31.850
What's on the opposit end of humility?

00:37:33.130 --> 00:37:34.070
Arrogance.

00:37:34.930 --> 00:37:36.960
Does Islam endorse arrogance?

00:37:37.730 --> 00:37:39.660
Does Islam encourage arrogance?

00:37:40.130 --> 00:37:41.150
Absolutely not.

00:37:41.630 --> 00:37:45.050
As a matter of fact, one of the worst things you can have inside of you is arrogance.

00:37:45.630 --> 00:37:48.350
Even if you have a little bit of it, you can't get into Jannah.

00:37:49.830 --> 00:37:52.380
But the problem is when so many Muslims

00:37:52.380 --> 00:37:55.550
in the world confuse arrogance with confidence.

00:37:57.130 --> 00:38:01.910
Islam is against arrogance. But
Islam is not against confidence.

00:38:02.620 --> 00:38:05.830
So what's the difference between arrogance and the confidence, you ask.

00:38:06.920 --> 00:38:08.311
Surah Yusuf can teach us.

00:38:09.520 --> 00:38:12.420
Yusuf (عليه السلام)-- before we talk about Yusuf (عليه السلام),

00:38:12.430 --> 00:38:14.040
let's let's actually give you an example.

00:38:14.050 --> 00:38:15.790
We used to, you know, in the United States,

00:38:15.790 --> 00:38:18.490
we have some states where there's a big Muslim population.

00:38:18.490 --> 00:38:20.060
New York has a big Muslim population.

00:38:20.070 --> 00:38:23.240
Houston has a big Muslim population.

00:38:23.240 --> 00:38:25.370
The state of California has a large Muslim population.

00:38:25.380 --> 00:38:29.340
But there are some states in the United States
where there's very small Muslim populations.

00:38:29.420 --> 00:38:32.070
There are some universities where like four Muslim students.

00:38:32.480 --> 00:38:34.570
Some universities have 4000 Muslim students.

00:38:34.570 --> 00:38:36.530
But some have maybe four or three Muslim students.

00:38:37.120 --> 00:38:40.520
So you go to one of these towns and there's like three Muslim students,

00:38:40.610 --> 00:38:42.460
and two of them don't even know how to pray.

00:38:42.460 --> 00:38:43.440
They pray in English.

00:38:44.520 --> 00:38:46.440
And one of them is a hafiz of Quran.

00:38:47.420 --> 00:38:49.450
One of them is at least a hafiz. He's not an 'aalim.

00:38:49.820 --> 00:38:51.950
He's not an 'aalim, but he's memorized the whole Quran.

00:38:52.320 --> 00:38:53.250
But he's very humble.

00:38:54.490 --> 00:38:56.340
There's no masjid in the entire town.

00:38:57.720 --> 00:39:00.750
So then jummah comes, they get together in one of the rooms in college,

00:39:01.220 --> 00:39:02.330
"We should have jummah prayer."

00:39:03.020 --> 00:39:05.650
And between the three of them, who should be leading the prayer?

00:39:06.640 --> 00:39:09.170
The hafiz of the Quran. But the hafiz of the Quran is a very humble guy.

00:39:10.820 --> 00:39:12.650
They ask him, "Bro, can you lead the prayer?"

00:39:13.920 --> 00:39:15.450
"No, ya akhi al-kareem."

00:39:16.220 --> 00:39:18.440
"I am nothing.
I am no one."

00:39:21.120 --> 00:39:27.530
"I do so much sin. I am not worthy to stand on
the mimbar of Rasoolullah (صلى الله عليه وسلم)."

00:39:28.920 --> 00:39:36.150
"You don't know how many sins I commit.
I am a filthy human being."

00:39:37.720 --> 00:39:42.450
And the other guy says, "Well,
I think you're a filthy human being, too."

00:39:43.720 --> 00:39:48.840
"But, the other guy will
lead the prayer in English."

00:39:49.620 --> 00:39:51.650
"Can you please lead the prayer, dude?"

00:39:53.980 --> 00:39:56.830
The problem with this young hafiz who is super humble

00:39:58.020 --> 00:40:00.320
is that he is confusing what with what?

00:40:01.710 --> 00:40:03.950
Arrogance with confidence.

00:40:04.020 --> 00:40:07.750
There are situations where Allah expects you to rise to the

00:40:07.750 --> 00:40:10.740
occasion and step up and be a man and be a woman.

00:40:11.510 --> 00:40:13.520
Because nobody else is gonna do it.

00:40:14.210 --> 00:40:15.230
Just do it.

00:40:16.410 --> 00:40:18.830
Look, the fact that I am coming here.

00:40:20.010 --> 00:40:22.520
In Malaysia
to speak to you

00:40:23.010 --> 00:40:27.530
about the Quran
is embarrassing to me.

00:40:29.410 --> 00:40:30.520
This is a Muslim country.

00:40:31.410 --> 00:40:32.940
I shouldn't be coming here to teach.

00:40:33.810 --> 00:40:35.030
I should be coming here to

00:40:35.710 --> 00:40:36.030
learn.

00:40:36.910 --> 00:40:40.630
There are people in the audience that know a hundred times more than I do. I guarantee it.

00:40:41.410 --> 00:40:43.440
About the book of Allah. I guarantee it. I have no doubt about it.

00:40:44.010 --> 00:40:46.250
There are people even in the United States,

00:40:46.260 --> 00:40:48.180
that have so much more knowledge than I do of the

00:40:48.180 --> 00:40:52.420
book of Allah that compared to me-- compared to them,

00:40:52.420 --> 00:40:53.730
I am not even a kindergartner.

00:40:54.310 --> 00:40:54.940
I'm not.

00:40:56.310 --> 00:40:59.230
So somebody says to me, "When there are so many more knowledgeable people than you,

00:40:59.230 --> 00:41:02.230
Why you open your mouth?
Why do you speak?"

00:41:03.210 --> 00:41:06.510
I say, "Because I have confidence

00:41:07.010 --> 00:41:09.530
in the fact,
not that I know more,

00:41:10.110 --> 00:41:14.730
but I have confidence in the fact that
people are benefiting from me teaching."

00:41:16.710 --> 00:41:17.330
Teaching.

00:41:17.810 --> 00:41:21.060
And I'm hoping that other teachers-- other scholars

00:41:21.510 --> 00:41:25.180
listen to some of me teaching and say to themselves,

00:41:25.180 --> 00:41:27.350
"What does this clown know about the Quran?

00:41:27.360 --> 00:41:28.640
Let me teach it."

00:41:29.410 --> 00:41:32.740
And then they teach it way better than I teach it and I'll say, "Okay, this is good."

00:41:32.760 --> 00:41:34.240
Now I'm not needed anymore.

00:41:35.510 --> 00:41:37.240
I wanna make myself irrelevant.

00:41:37.730 --> 00:41:38.140
I do.

00:41:39.110 --> 00:41:42.090
My hopes with my own students are they go way further

00:41:42.090 --> 00:41:44.930
than I go because the bar has to be raised.

00:41:46.110 --> 00:41:51.170
But I am confident in what I'm doing now because - and I'll tell you why -

00:41:51.180 --> 00:41:52.640
because of Surah Yusuf.

00:41:53.910 --> 00:41:56.940
Yusuf (عليه السلام) is very humble in his childhood. You remember this?

00:41:58.010 --> 00:41:59.170
He comes out of jail.

00:41:59.310 --> 00:42:00.620
He interprets a dream.

00:42:01.500 --> 00:42:04.620
He interprets the king's dream. You remember this? He interprets the king's dream.

00:42:04.620 --> 00:42:07.920
Now they bring them to court. His innocence is proven.

00:42:08.700 --> 00:42:12.670
And they find out that there is going to be a major economic crisis for seven years.

00:42:12.670 --> 00:42:15.680
There's not gonna be any food available. We have to ration the supplies.

00:42:15.680 --> 00:42:20.370
If you don't manage this economic crisis carefully, people will starve to death.

00:42:20.370 --> 00:42:23.940
The entire society could crumble. The empire could be destroyed.

00:42:23.950 --> 00:42:27.090
This is a very serious matter for the entire nation.

00:42:27.100 --> 00:42:29.358
The right man is needed for the job.

00:42:29.378 --> 00:42:33.720
Yusuf (عليه السلام) looks around the court of the king and says, "Well, these ministers,

00:42:34.100 --> 00:42:36.110
yeah, they're all idiots. Why don't you hire me?"

00:42:37.290 --> 00:42:41.648
قَالَ ٱجۡعَلۡنِی عَلَىٰ خَزَاۤىِٕنِ ٱلۡأَرۡضِ، إِنِّی حَفِیظٌ عَلِیمࣱ

00:42:41.900 --> 00:42:46.310
Make me responsible over the treasury of the entire country.

00:42:46.800 --> 00:42:48.810
Make me the national treasurer.

00:42:49.200 --> 00:42:51.280
Make me the Treasury Secretary.

00:42:51.450 --> 00:42:52.920
He nominated who?

00:42:53.600 --> 00:42:56.530
Himself. The king didn't say, "Hey, could you please do this job?"

00:42:56.530 --> 00:42:59.550
And he said, "No, please, I am just a prisoner."

00:43:00.070 --> 00:43:01.010
No, no, no.

00:43:02.300 --> 00:43:04.630
And by the way, what are his qualifications?

00:43:04.640 --> 00:43:09.280
Has he gone to an elite university to understand economics and finance?

00:43:09.290 --> 00:43:13.960
Has he done that? No. Where did he spend a lot of his youth? As a servant.

00:43:13.970 --> 00:43:15.820
Where did he spend the rest of his youth?

00:43:16.300 --> 00:43:17.240
As a prisoner.

00:43:17.320 --> 00:43:19.460
And now he's standing in front of a king and saying,

00:43:19.460 --> 00:43:21.010
"I need to be the Treasury Secretary."

00:43:22.500 --> 00:43:25.320
Do you understand the confidence of this man when he's speaking?

00:43:26.800 --> 00:43:27.370
Why?

00:43:27.370 --> 00:43:32.360
Because he says, "There are two qualifications you people need for this job,

00:43:32.370 --> 00:43:34.030
and it's not a PhD in economics.

00:43:34.040 --> 00:43:37.190
What you people need is someone who will take their job seriously,

00:43:37.200 --> 00:43:40.120
"[حَفِيظ]". And secondly, you'll need someone

00:43:40.500 --> 00:43:41.820
who will be honest."

00:43:42.300 --> 00:43:45.120
"And honestly, you don't. You have politicians in the room.

00:43:48.800 --> 00:43:49.820
I'm the right guy for the job."

00:43:51.400 --> 00:43:52.930
He nominated himself.

00:43:54.000 --> 00:43:56.980
When nobody else is there to take up the task,

00:43:56.990 --> 00:44:01.580
and you know that Allah has given you a gift that you can use to help other people,

00:44:01.590 --> 00:44:03.590
then you don't say "No, no. I'm nothing.

00:44:03.590 --> 00:44:06.110
I'm no one. I'm a mosquito. I'm a cockroach." No, no, no.

00:44:08.390 --> 00:44:09.310
You do it.

00:44:09.890 --> 00:44:12.010
You step up to the plate and you do it.

00:44:13.390 --> 00:44:15.550
Let me then tell you what arrogance is.

00:44:15.584 --> 00:44:18.430
May Allah protect all of us from arrogance. Starting with myself.

00:44:18.790 --> 00:44:20.810
What is arrogance? Arrogance is two things.

00:44:21.080 --> 00:44:23.110
One, when you are impressed with yourself.

00:44:23.590 --> 00:44:26.500
And two, when you think of yourself as better than others.

00:44:26.990 --> 00:44:28.680
Those are the two problems of arrogance.

00:44:30.190 --> 00:44:32.050
None of us should be impressed with ourselves,

00:44:32.060 --> 00:44:34.300
but that doesn't mean we deny the gifts of Allah gave us.

00:44:35.690 --> 00:44:38.120
I have no shame in saying I think Allah made me a good teacher.

00:44:38.460 --> 00:44:39.410
I have no shame in saying it.

00:44:40.290 --> 00:44:43.230
But I also have no shame in saying that I have lots and lots of flaws.

00:44:43.240 --> 00:44:45.190
If you want to know a list of them, email my wife,

00:44:45.190 --> 00:44:48.190
she'll tell you. She's got a lot. She's pretty much written a book on it.

00:44:48.190 --> 00:44:49.310
And she's got a long list.

00:44:49.990 --> 00:44:50.310
Okay?

00:44:50.990 --> 00:44:54.170
My father can tell you my flaws. My mother can tell you my flaws.

00:44:54.180 --> 00:44:56.740
And if you want to protect yourself from arrogance,

00:44:56.750 --> 00:44:58.270
let me give you some personal advice.

00:44:58.270 --> 00:45:00.800
This is not from the Quran and Sunnah. It's personal advice.

00:45:01.290 --> 00:45:02.930
How do you protect yourself from arrogance?

00:45:02.940 --> 00:45:05.910
You have to be around people who are not impressed with you.

00:45:08.790 --> 00:45:09.720
Which means your mother.

00:45:12.790 --> 00:45:13.800
[laughs]

00:45:15.090 --> 00:45:17.100
If you spend time with your mother, you will stay humble.

00:45:18.690 --> 00:45:21.430
For young men, if you really want to be humble,

00:45:21.680 --> 00:45:22.610
spend time with your dad.

00:45:23.190 --> 00:45:25.220
because you will be a loser as long as you live.

00:45:25.590 --> 00:45:26.510
With your dad.

00:45:27.090 --> 00:45:27.810
You're a loser.

00:45:28.990 --> 00:45:34.600
You can finish your PhD and he said, "When I was your age, I had four PhDs."

00:45:36.690 --> 00:45:38.910
He will never be satisfied with you.

00:45:39.390 --> 00:45:40.800
You are never good enough.

00:45:41.790 --> 00:45:46.580
So you want a humility check? Just give your dad a call and talk to him for 15 minutes

00:45:47.590 --> 00:45:49.300
It will bring you back to earth.

00:45:49.690 --> 00:45:51.220
Okay? [laughs] So-

00:45:52.390 --> 00:45:56.710
but the balance, the incredible balance between humility on the one end-- Because,

00:45:56.720 --> 00:45:59.020
you know, in the people doing sajda to him

00:45:59.490 --> 00:46:01.590
it is as though he is better than other people.

00:46:02.280 --> 00:46:05.910
If he accepted that, that would be arrogance. He had a problem with that.

00:46:05.920 --> 00:46:08.160
But when it came to helping other people and

00:46:08.160 --> 00:46:10.640
stepping up to the plate and taking responsibility,

00:46:10.640 --> 00:46:12.300
then you gotta do what you gotta do.

00:46:13.580 --> 00:46:14.410
You know?

00:46:14.880 --> 00:46:16.410
People come to me all the time.

00:46:16.980 --> 00:46:20.210
I had a student this year. It was really interesting. I had a student this year.

00:46:20.220 --> 00:46:22.410
A young lady from England.

00:46:22.880 --> 00:46:25.210
"Ustaad, what am I going to do when I go back?"

00:46:27.480 --> 00:46:28.230
[laughs]

00:46:33.580 --> 00:46:37.550
"I want to stay here in Texas because there's nobody there to learn from.

00:46:37.560 --> 00:46:38.910
There's nothing to do there."

00:46:41.480 --> 00:46:45.700
I know it's terrible,
but

00:46:46.480 --> 00:46:47.290
you know what I told her?

00:46:48.250 --> 00:46:49.230
I told her

00:46:50.080 --> 00:46:52.900
"Uh there's nothing to do there because you're not there."

00:46:55.040 --> 00:46:56.990
"There's no activities for women there."

00:46:57.970 --> 00:46:59.910
I said, "They're not there cos you're here."

00:47:00.880 --> 00:47:01.990
"Go there."

00:47:04.280 --> 00:47:05.410
[laughs]

00:47:07.780 --> 00:47:10.010
You need to do something yourself.

00:47:10.130 --> 00:47:12.430
We keep waiting for someone to come and help us.

00:47:14.380 --> 00:47:18.220
You know, this is actually, this is a true story. I used to be like that.

00:47:18.230 --> 00:47:20.760
I used to complain. "Why do you think we don't have good leaders?

00:47:20.760 --> 00:47:22.850
Why do you think we don't have any good activities at the masjid.

00:47:22.860 --> 00:47:25.520
Why do you think there aren't enough youth programs? Why do you think there isn't this?

00:47:25.520 --> 00:47:27.520
Why do you think there isn't that?" And one of my mentors

00:47:27.520 --> 00:47:31.740
I still remember. One of my older brothers, you know, in deen, in learning.

00:47:31.750 --> 00:47:33.490
He grabbed my arm one time. He goes, "Nouman,"

00:47:33.960 --> 00:47:36.800
and he was Pakistani, he had a good Pakistani accent. He goes, "Nouman,

00:47:37.180 --> 00:47:38.710
if you cannot find the man,

00:47:39.480 --> 00:47:40.910
you had to be the man."

00:47:44.050 --> 00:47:46.490
[laughs]

00:47:47.380 --> 00:47:49.490
I was like, "Okay, I'll be the man."

00:47:49.490 --> 00:47:51.990
[laughs]

00:47:52.080 --> 00:47:53.400
But that's what I tell you guys too.

00:47:54.180 --> 00:47:54.990
We have to step up.

00:47:55.680 --> 00:47:57.410
We have to stop hiding behind excuses.

00:47:57.980 --> 00:47:59.500
You know? It's time we do that.

00:48:00.270 --> 00:48:03.870
I did want to give you one more example of the structure of surahs. We did talk about

00:48:03.892 --> 00:48:06.600
Surah Yusuf. Maybe one more example and I'll give you your next break.

00:48:06.600 --> 00:48:09.590
InshaaAllah. And perhaps the example I will give you--

00:48:10.470 --> 00:48:13.160
Uh, which one should I pick? Okay, let's take Surah al-Hijr.

00:48:14.370 --> 00:48:16.080
It's actually a really interesting example.

00:48:16.670 --> 00:48:20.720
Uh, here, the structure of a surah can be studied from many angles.

00:48:20.730 --> 00:48:24.280
But one angle I'd like to talk to you about is the beginning and the end of a surah.

00:48:24.290 --> 00:48:29.000
Meaning, the way a surah begins it is somehow correlated with the way a surah ends.

00:48:29.670 --> 00:48:32.490
Those two things go hand in hand with each other, okay? So,

00:48:33.070 --> 00:48:34.475
in Surah al-Hijr, Allah says

00:48:34.495 --> 00:48:37.515
الۤرۚ تِلۡكَ ءَایَـٰتُ ٱلۡكِتَـٰبِ وَقُرۡءَانࣲ مُّبِینࣲ

00:48:37.525 --> 00:48:38.555
Let me translate that for you.

00:48:38.575 --> 00:48:41.760
Alif, laam, raa. Those are the miraculous signs - the aayaat -

00:48:41.920 --> 00:48:45.090
of the book and a clear and clarifying Quran.

00:48:45.770 --> 00:48:47.770
This gives me an opportunity to talk to you about

00:48:47.780 --> 00:48:50.810
a very important concept in Arabic and the Quran.

00:48:51.030 --> 00:48:52.580
The Quran is clear.

00:48:53.070 --> 00:48:55.120
The Quran is clear.

00:48:55.240 --> 00:48:57.290
But the Quran is not simple.

00:48:58.770 --> 00:49:01.910
The Quran is clear, but the Quran is not simple.

00:49:01.920 --> 00:49:06.280
Some people come up to me and ask me sometimes, "Allah says that the Quran is easy."

00:49:06.290 --> 00:49:11.230
"The Quran is simple. Then why do you give such elaborate linguistic explanations?"

00:49:11.230 --> 00:49:12.900
"You're supposed to keep it simple."

00:49:13.470 --> 00:49:16.400
"If it's so simple. How is it so hard to understand?"

00:49:17.070 --> 00:49:18.540
And they use the word simple.

00:49:18.650 --> 00:49:20.480
And I have a problem with the usage of that word

00:49:20.480 --> 00:49:22.500
because Allah never used that word in the Quran.

00:49:22.970 --> 00:49:24.890
Allah did use the word clear, though, [مُبِين].

00:49:25.370 --> 00:49:26.590
Clear and clarifying.

00:49:27.170 --> 00:49:29.160
Now what is the difference between clear and

00:49:29.340 --> 00:49:33.590
simple? When I say two plus two equals four, that is clear, and it is

00:49:33.970 --> 00:49:36.880
simple. Now, if a PhD in calculus

00:49:36.990 --> 00:49:42.790
solves a major mathematical problem on the board that takes four pages,

00:49:43.370 --> 00:49:46.230
it takes up the entire board, and he solves a calculus problem

00:49:46.350 --> 00:49:50.780
for a student of calculus who is good, his solution is clear.

00:49:51.470 --> 00:49:54.500
But his solution is still not
simple.

00:49:55.270 --> 00:49:59.760
Clarity has nothing to do with
simplicity. These are two different things.

00:49:59.770 --> 00:50:03.170
Clarity is about whether or not your answer

00:50:03.170 --> 00:50:05.690
makes sense to someone who thinks about it.

00:50:06.660 --> 00:50:12.650
So for a medical student, his advanced medical terms are very clear to him.

00:50:12.660 --> 00:50:15.080
Even though the terms themselves are not simple.

00:50:15.080 --> 00:50:17.270
You understand? Those are two distinct things.

00:50:17.280 --> 00:50:19.490
The Quran is clear, but it is not

00:50:20.050 --> 00:50:20.660
simple.

00:50:20.770 --> 00:50:24.530
Why? Because the Quran solves very complex problems.

00:50:24.960 --> 00:50:27.560
Humanity has complex problems, and Allah gave

00:50:27.570 --> 00:50:30.620
sometimes complex solutions to those complex problems.

00:50:30.790 --> 00:50:33.780
The idea in the Quran is not that those solutions are simple,

00:50:33.790 --> 00:50:37.080
but the idea certainly is that those solutions are clear.

00:50:37.860 --> 00:50:41.490
Here's another issue here. Let's add one more bit to this problem.

00:50:43.160 --> 00:50:45.890
But Allah does say that Allah made the Quran easy.

00:50:46.660 --> 00:50:48.290
وَلَقَدۡ یَسَّرۡنَا ٱلۡقُرۡءَانَ لِلذِّكۡرِ

00:50:48.310 --> 00:50:50.340
Didn't He? He said He made the Quran easy.

00:50:51.260 --> 00:50:54.470
So how come it's not easy? Well, He didn't just say He made it easy.

00:50:54.480 --> 00:50:57.640
He said He made it easy for remembrance.

00:50:57.650 --> 00:51:00.930
If you want to remember Allah, if you want to do dhikr of Allah,

00:51:00.940 --> 00:51:04.330
if you want to gain some advice, if you want to memorize, then

00:51:04.350 --> 00:51:05.480
the Quran is easy.

00:51:06.260 --> 00:51:09.190
But if you want to dive into the depths, that's not when He said it's easy.

00:51:09.200 --> 00:51:12.600
He put the ease of the Quran associated with the remembrance of Allah.

00:51:12.610 --> 00:51:14.920
So it's easy for you to memorize the Fatihah.

00:51:14.930 --> 00:51:18.544
It's easy for you to remember the lessons of,
وَٱلۡعَصۡرِ، إِنَّ ٱلۡإِنسَـٰنَ لَفِی خُسۡرٍ

00:51:18.550 --> 00:51:22.990
It's easy for you when you want to remember and get some advice from the Quran.

00:51:23.460 --> 00:51:25.190
He facilitated it for that reason.

00:51:25.760 --> 00:51:27.444
That's,
وَلَقَدۡ یَسَّرۡنَا ٱلۡقُرۡءَانَ لِلذِّكۡرِ

00:51:27.450 --> 00:51:31.880
Anyway, the beginning of the surah says that these are aayaat of a clear book

00:51:32.760 --> 00:51:34.080
and a clear Quran.

00:51:34.560 --> 00:51:36.890
Okay, what is the end say.

00:51:36.890 --> 00:51:39.290
Well here's something that can destroy the Quran's clarity.

00:51:39.322 --> 00:51:41.622
ٱلَّذِینَ جَعَلُوا۟ ٱلۡقُرۡءَانَ عِضِینَ

00:51:41.642 --> 00:51:44.052
The people who took the Quran and tore it to pieces.

00:51:44.060 --> 00:51:44.920
In other words,

00:51:44.930 --> 00:51:48.000
an attack against the clarity of the Quran is

00:51:48.000 --> 00:51:49.920
that you look at some ideas from over here,

00:51:49.930 --> 00:51:51.780
but you don't look at the rest of the aayahs.

00:51:52.060 --> 00:51:55.500
If you take a piece of the Quran and not the other pieces of the Quran,

00:51:55.500 --> 00:51:58.390
and come to a conclusion, then that will remove its

00:51:58.860 --> 00:51:59.490
clarity.

00:52:00.050 --> 00:52:02.370
So the subject matter of the Quran's clarity is

00:52:02.370 --> 00:52:05.290
actually completely covered from beginning to the end.

00:52:05.300 --> 00:52:08.160
Then Allah says in the beginning of the surah, very interestingly,

00:52:08.170 --> 00:52:14.170
رُّبَمَا یَوَدُّ ٱلَّذِینَ كَفَرُوا۟ لَوۡ كَانُوا۟ مُسۡلِمِینَ

00:52:14.170 --> 00:52:17.110
Perhaps the Disbelievers will wish that they were Muslims.

00:52:17.120 --> 00:52:19.080
When will they wish that they were Muslims?

00:52:19.090 --> 00:52:22.070
Disbelievers are going to wish that they were Muslims? When will that happen?

00:52:23.250 --> 00:52:24.714
Judgment Day. Which is why at the end,

00:52:24.714 --> 00:52:27.214
فَوَرَبِّكَ لَنَسۡـَٔلَنَّهُمۡ أَجۡمَعِینَ

00:52:27.230 --> 00:52:30.620
I swear to your Master we will interrogate all of them.

00:52:31.050 --> 00:52:34.370
And by the way, when the interrogation begins on Judgment Day, what will they wish?

00:52:35.450 --> 00:52:36.480
That they were Muslims.

00:52:36.920 --> 00:52:38.270
Then He says in the beginning,

00:52:38.730 --> 00:52:40.246
ذَرۡهُمۡ
Leave them alone,

00:52:40.276 --> 00:52:44.246
یَأۡكُلُوا۟ وَیَتَمَتَّعُوا۟ وَیُلۡهِهِمُ ٱلۡأَمَلُۖ فَسَوۡفَ یَعۡلَمُونَ

00:52:44.246 --> 00:52:46.126
Let them eat and enjoy.

00:52:46.150 --> 00:52:48.180
Let them do whatever they want,

00:52:48.750 --> 00:52:51.870
and let their false hopes confuse them and delude them,

00:52:52.550 --> 00:52:56.410
and mislead them. They'll soon find out. What will they find out?

00:52:56.410 --> 00:52:58.170
عَمَّا كَانُوا۟ یَعۡمَلُونَ

00:52:58.190 --> 00:53:00.730
They'll find out the things they used to do.

00:53:00.750 --> 00:53:03.230
We will interrogate them about the things they used to do.

00:53:03.490 --> 00:53:04.860
Now what are the things they used to do?

00:53:04.860 --> 00:53:08.370
The aayah tells us in the beginning, they used to eat, and enjoy, and be deluded.

00:53:08.950 --> 00:53:10.190
That's what they used to do.

00:53:10.200 --> 00:53:14.050
My favorite correlation, though, is at the end. The Prophet (صلى الله عليه وسلم)

00:53:14.070 --> 00:53:15.370
used to be made fun of.

00:53:15.850 --> 00:53:18.340
They used to insult the Prophet (صلى الله عليه وسلم).

00:53:18.350 --> 00:53:19.250
They used to say,

00:53:19.250 --> 00:53:22.710
وَقَالُوا۟ یَـٰۤأَیُّهَا ٱلَّذِی نُزِّلَ عَلَیۡهِ ٱلذِّكۡرُ إِنَّكَ لَمَجۡنُونࣱ

00:53:22.720 --> 00:53:27.070
Hey, you! The one who the reminder comes to. You're crazy.

00:53:28.450 --> 00:53:29.670
That's how I'm translating the aayah. Hey, you!

00:53:29.690 --> 00:53:33.900
Hey, you! The one who reminder comes to. The dhikr comes to you, right?

00:53:33.910 --> 00:53:35.880
Let me tell you, you're insane.

00:53:36.650 --> 00:53:40.070
You're possessed by a jinn. And at the end of the surah, what does Allah say?

00:53:40.650 --> 00:53:43.290
Allah says to the Prophet (صلى الله عليه وسلم)-- Now in the beginning

00:53:43.290 --> 00:53:44.670
the Kuffar were talking to him.

00:53:45.550 --> 00:53:46.400
At the end,

00:53:46.400 --> 00:53:48.900
إِنَّا كَفَیۡنَـٰكَ ٱلۡمُسۡتَهۡزِءِینَ

00:53:48.900 --> 00:53:53.830
وَلَقَدۡ نَعۡلَمُ أَنَّكَ یَضِیقُ صَدۡرُكَ بِمَا یَقُولُونَ

00:53:53.850 --> 00:53:56.070
We are enough against you.

00:53:56.450 --> 00:54:00.670
We are enough for you against all of those who make fun of you.

00:54:01.440 --> 00:54:02.760
I'll take care of them for you.

00:54:03.340 --> 00:54:05.260
Who are the ones who made fun of him?

00:54:05.430 --> 00:54:06.360
When are they mentioned?

00:54:07.130 --> 00:54:09.670
In the beginning. And at the end, Allah says, I'll take care of them.

00:54:10.640 --> 00:54:11.701
And then Allah also says,

00:54:11.701 --> 00:54:15.725
وَلَقَدۡ نَعۡلَمُ أَنَّكَ یَضِیقُ صَدۡرُكَ بِمَا یَقُولُونَ

00:54:15.790 --> 00:54:18.415
We already know that your chest hurts.

00:54:18.440 --> 00:54:19.530
Your heart hurts.

00:54:19.800 --> 00:54:22.970
You get bad feelings in your heart because of what they say.

00:54:23.640 --> 00:54:24.980
That's mentioned at the end. Now,

00:54:24.980 --> 00:54:28.050
Allah doesn't say what they say at the end, because He already said that where?

00:54:28.940 --> 00:54:30.670
In the beginning and what is it that they say?

00:54:31.640 --> 00:54:32.560
That he's insane.

00:54:33.340 --> 00:54:34.970
So surahs-- even long surahs

00:54:34.970 --> 00:54:38.590
you'll find a beautiful correlation between the beginning and the end.

00:54:38.600 --> 00:54:40.910
Subject matters are tied like that, and by the way,

00:54:40.910 --> 00:54:44.110
that's good practice for a teacher, because teachers,

00:54:44.110 --> 00:54:47.110
if they know what they're doing when they start a class, they introduce the lesson,

00:54:47.120 --> 00:54:49.960
and when they end the class, they go over what they covered in the beginning.

00:54:51.040 --> 00:54:54.380
Before they tie up the lesson, they kind of do a quick review and they move on, right?

00:54:54.390 --> 00:54:57.030
So that's supposed to be a teaching methodology anyway,

00:54:57.030 --> 00:54:59.760
and it's captured and encapsulated inside the Quran.